# One line ending in the repository, whatever the checkout platform does.
#
# Git warned on every file here about LF becoming CRLF, because the repository had no rule and the
# working copy is on Windows. Left alone, that rewrites every line of every file on the first checkout
# elsewhere, which buries real changes in noise. `text=auto` normalises into the repository and
# `eol=lf` keeps the working copy consistent for the tools that read these files as text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Tarballs are packed here and installed from a path, so a line-ending rewrite would change their
# bytes and invalidate the checksum a lockfile records.
*.tgz -text

# Binary test fixtures must never be normalised.
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.zstd -text
